1
00:00:05,520 --> 00:00:10,570
The Battle of Ketil's Farm

2
00:00:08,840 --> 00:00:11,190
There's about 350 here.

3
00:00:11,690 --> 00:00:15,260
Only around 100 of them
will be any good in a fight.

4
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:18,910
Get an exact head count later.

5
00:00:20,470 --> 00:00:24,330
Are we really doing this, boss?

6
00:00:25,350 --> 00:00:28,340
The master insists on fighting.

7
00:00:28,340 --> 00:00:29,730
We have no choice.

8
00:00:32,950 --> 00:00:35,550
They're out of their minds.

9
00:00:36,310 --> 00:00:40,720
Do they think they stand a chance
against the king's forces?

10
00:00:41,590 --> 00:00:45,040
They all owe money to the master.

11
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:49,470
They were told he'd cancel their debts
if they fought in the battle.

12
00:00:50,410 --> 00:00:54,620
If they'd known they'd be fighting the king,
they probably wouldn't have shown up.

13
00:00:54,620 --> 00:00:59,290
But now that they're here, their vanity
as Norse men won't allow them to leave.

14
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:03,840
And the more of them there are,
the bolder they get.

15
00:01:04,370 --> 00:01:06,720
They start feeling like
they could actually win.

16
00:01:07,150 --> 00:01:10,670
Waiting until they were gathered
to tell them they'd be fighting the king

17
00:01:10,670 --> 00:01:12,550
was a smart choice.

18
00:01:15,630 --> 00:01:20,030
Thorgil's a better strategist
than I expected.

19
00:01:40,270 --> 00:01:41,790
The master intends to fight.

20
00:01:42,290 --> 00:01:44,200
The soldiers have gathered.

21
00:01:45,340 --> 00:01:48,160
This place will become a battlefield.

22
00:01:49,780 --> 00:01:51,990
See? It's just like we told you.

23
00:01:51,990 --> 00:01:56,590
We need to leave this farm right away,
or we'll get caught up in it, Thorfinn.

24
00:01:57,290 --> 00:02:00,090
I know, but...

25
00:02:09,980 --> 00:02:11,410
Mister Leif.

26
00:02:13,630 --> 00:02:19,610
We can't leave the farm with
Arnheid in this condition, sir.

27
00:02:21,750 --> 00:02:28,670
Thank you for caring about me.

28
00:02:31,770 --> 00:02:34,130
You've changed, Thorfinn.

29
00:02:35,270 --> 00:02:38,650
When I first saw you,
I thought you were someone else.

30
00:02:42,350 --> 00:02:46,060
The look on your face is
better these days, Thorfinn.

31
00:02:51,660 --> 00:02:54,000
I finally got to see you.

32
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:58,970
I can't leave without you.

33
00:03:01,510 --> 00:03:03,060
Mr. Pater, she's coughing again.

34
00:03:03,060 --> 00:03:04,820
Roll her onto her side.

35
00:03:04,820 --> 00:03:07,230
Don't let her choke on anything she spits up.

36
00:03:08,650 --> 00:03:13,920
Pater, would it be possible to move Arnheid?

37
00:03:14,830 --> 00:03:18,510
We should be cautious with her now.

38
00:03:19,160 --> 00:03:22,960
We'd know how she's doing if she'd wake up,

39
00:03:23,630 --> 00:03:29,050
but honestly, not even I can tell
her condition right now.

40
00:03:30,140 --> 00:03:33,450
There's also the child inside her to consider.

41
00:03:33,870 --> 00:03:37,140
Rest is the what she needs most right now,

42
00:03:37,140 --> 00:03:40,190
at least until she regains consciousness.

43
00:03:42,630 --> 00:03:48,400
One day. Let's wait and see
how things go for just one more day.

44
00:03:49,300 --> 00:03:51,520
Are you serious?

45
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:54,080
What about after that?

46
00:04:03,020 --> 00:04:05,050
Boss, hurry.

47
00:04:06,310 --> 00:04:07,460
North?

48
00:04:07,460 --> 00:04:08,310
Yes.

49
00:04:09,110 --> 00:04:10,800
Where I'm pointing.

50
00:04:15,980 --> 00:04:17,950
They're here sooner than expected.

51
00:04:18,950 --> 00:04:20,470
Notify the master!

52
00:04:20,470 --> 00:04:22,650
Ships have been spotted
in the sea to the north!

53
00:04:23,980 --> 00:04:27,230
The king's forces have arrived.

54
00:06:15,560 --> 00:06:17,810
Idiot, don't shoot unless you're told to!

55
00:06:18,190 --> 00:06:20,770
You'll never reach them at this range.

56
00:06:21,070 --> 00:06:23,770
Once they're closer, we'll fire off a—

57
00:06:36,950 --> 00:06:40,170
Crap! Retreat, retreat!

58
00:06:40,980 --> 00:06:42,210
Damn it!

59
00:06:42,640 --> 00:06:45,230
How are they reaching us from so far away?

60
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:57,730
Fan out and take control of the area!

61
00:06:57,730 --> 00:07:00,100
Aid His Majesty's landing!

62
00:07:10,870 --> 00:07:14,830
It seems Ketil intends to fight me.

63
00:07:16,170 --> 00:07:18,420
Send a messenger, Ulf.

64
00:07:18,420 --> 00:07:21,970
We'll take up position here
and await Ketil's response.

65
00:07:21,970 --> 00:07:22,860
Yes, Your Majesty.

66
00:07:28,140 --> 00:07:29,520
This is good land.

67
00:07:30,190 --> 00:07:32,250
It'd be a shame to stain it with blood.

68
00:07:41,550 --> 00:07:45,440
For the aforementioned reasons,
His Majesty, King Canute

69
00:07:45,440 --> 00:07:52,990
has sentenced the insurrectionist Ketil
and his clan to ten years of outlawry.

70
00:07:53,580 --> 00:07:57,390
Though normally they would be
executed for their crimes,

71
00:07:57,390 --> 00:08:04,610
Ketil's clan shall be allowed to live
thanks to His Majesty's kindness.

72
00:08:04,610 --> 00:08:07,050
Humbly accept your punishment.

73
00:08:10,070 --> 00:08:14,630
That's all. If you don't want to die,
then get out of the country.

74
00:08:14,630 --> 00:08:17,470
We'll wait until tomorrow morning
for your response.

75
00:08:25,400 --> 00:08:29,400
How could you useless lot
let them land without a fight?

76
00:08:31,150 --> 00:08:34,660
Insurrectionist? Outlawry?

77
00:08:34,660 --> 00:08:38,030
Don't push your luck, boy.

78
00:08:38,790 --> 00:08:40,490
I'm back.

79
00:08:41,410 --> 00:08:45,920
Ah, Thorgil. How did Canute's forces look?

80
00:08:46,890 --> 00:08:50,550
They were cooking and eating
their lunch at leisure.

81
00:08:51,310 --> 00:08:54,310
Two warships, two cargo ships.

82
00:08:54,310 --> 00:08:57,680
They've pitched tents
right next to their landing site.

83
00:08:57,680 --> 00:09:00,560
There are about 100 of them.

84
00:09:02,630 --> 00:09:04,160
100?

85
00:09:04,160 --> 00:09:07,490
Yeah, excluding slaves and servants.

86
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:18,700
That's less than a third of our numbers.

87
00:09:19,310 --> 00:09:26,350
Did Canute think we'd kneel
if the king himself came?

88
00:09:26,870 --> 00:09:31,980
This land is full of reckless men
who won't yield to the king.

89
00:09:32,460 --> 00:09:34,910
Muster your courage, men!

90
00:09:34,910 --> 00:09:40,050
Whoever brings me the king's head
will receive whatever he wants!

91
00:09:43,320 --> 00:09:45,170
What fools.

92
00:09:47,750 --> 00:09:49,870
That's not just any 100 men.

93
00:09:51,370 --> 00:09:56,720
The guys around the big tent are thegns.

94
00:09:57,710 --> 00:10:01,370
Y-You mean the king's really here?

95
00:10:02,470 --> 00:10:08,170
And if they're the king's guard,
they're among the strongest men in Denmark.

96
00:10:08,670 --> 00:10:11,260
They're Thorgil's former brothers-in-arms.

97
00:10:12,050 --> 00:10:15,200
I-In other words,

98
00:10:15,980 --> 00:10:19,580
they're all about as strong as Thorgil?

99
00:10:20,750 --> 00:10:24,590
Wh-What about the guys in white capes?

100
00:10:24,590 --> 00:10:27,540
Are they weaker than the king's guard?

101
00:10:27,540 --> 00:10:30,510
You mean you've never seen them before?

102
00:10:31,670 --> 00:10:34,610
Those are Jomsvikings.

103
00:10:38,550 --> 00:10:42,410
I've never seen you
open your eyes so wide before.

104
00:10:46,280 --> 00:10:48,780
We can't beat them.

105
00:10:50,630 --> 00:10:55,810
They far outclass our ragtag
group of peasant soldiers.

106
00:10:55,810 --> 00:11:00,710
They're the kind of guys who think about war
and nothing else from morning 'til night.

107
00:11:01,870 --> 00:11:05,870
The master won't understand that
until we fight them once.

108
00:11:08,030 --> 00:11:10,500
If you want to run, then run.

109
00:11:10,500 --> 00:11:13,520
King Canute has given us time to flee.

110
00:11:14,600 --> 00:11:17,820
B-Boss, what are you going to do?

111
00:11:18,540 --> 00:11:21,700
I'm the commander. I can't run.

112
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:29,070
I'll do my best to keep as many of
those 350 cocky idiots alive as I can.

113
00:11:29,970 --> 00:11:36,270
Th-Then let's tie up Ketil's clan
and hand them over.

114
00:11:36,270 --> 00:11:39,460
Yeah, then we won't have to fight.

115
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:42,580
Are we going to tie up Thorgil, too?

116
00:11:42,580 --> 00:11:46,370
Don't be a wuss.
I bet eight of us could take him.

117
00:11:46,370 --> 00:11:49,220
Thorgil isn't the only problem.

118
00:11:49,650 --> 00:11:52,480
There's also the renowned Iron Fist Ketil.

119
00:11:52,480 --> 00:11:55,860
You heard he beat a bear to
death with his bare hands, right?

120
00:11:59,020 --> 00:12:02,630
Run away with us, boss.

121
00:12:02,630 --> 00:12:06,010
There's no point in being stubborn.

122
00:12:08,910 --> 00:12:10,750
Iron Fist, huh?

123
00:12:12,150 --> 00:12:15,290
I know all about the Iron Fist.

124
00:12:17,100 --> 00:12:19,710
I met him when I was around 15 or 16.

125
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:23,620
He taught me how to fight on the battlefield.

126
00:12:23,620 --> 00:12:26,460
He was insanely strong.

127
00:12:27,880 --> 00:12:31,520
He was like an older brother or boss to me.

128
00:12:33,890 --> 00:12:38,100
Years ago, I screwed up.

129
00:12:38,100 --> 00:12:40,400
I ended up on the run.

130
00:12:41,070 --> 00:12:44,900
I thought Ketil would shelter me.

131
00:12:44,900 --> 00:12:49,090
I followed the rumors to this farm.

132
00:12:50,750 --> 00:12:55,500
But when I finally arrived...

133
00:12:56,650 --> 00:13:00,000
Who are you? Do you have business with me?

134
00:13:01,110 --> 00:13:04,780
...I found a completely different person.

135
00:13:08,260 --> 00:13:11,520
Wh-What? Seriously?

136
00:13:12,470 --> 00:13:15,260
The master's full of shit.

137
00:13:15,260 --> 00:13:18,520
He's taking advantage of the fact
that they share the same name.

138
00:13:20,010 --> 00:13:21,550
That's appalling.

139
00:13:21,550 --> 00:13:24,400
I'm amazed he's never been
exposed before now.

140
00:13:24,790 --> 00:13:31,830
With nowhere else to go,
I've stayed here as his guard dog.

141
00:13:33,540 --> 00:13:36,560
I've been getting a free ride
for long enough.

142
00:13:38,230 --> 00:13:41,610
It's time to pay my tab.

143
00:13:52,920 --> 00:13:55,640
You boys do what you want.

144
00:13:55,640 --> 00:14:00,380
All I meant is that the master is
a con artist not worth dying for.

145
00:14:03,750 --> 00:14:05,900
Take care.

146
00:14:26,810 --> 00:14:29,490
Don't try to show off, idiots.

147
00:14:29,490 --> 00:14:32,930
You'll die before you get
the chance to pay off your tabs.

148
00:14:32,930 --> 00:14:34,960
Sh-Sh-Shut up!

149
00:14:35,980 --> 00:14:42,690
Dine-and-dashing on a con artist
would make us absolute scumbags.

150
00:14:42,690 --> 00:14:45,900
We'll work to earn our board.

151
00:14:49,150 --> 00:14:52,830
Don't go telling anyone else
what I just told you.

152
00:15:22,710 --> 00:15:25,230
Their backs are to the sea.

153
00:15:25,230 --> 00:15:28,220
The king's forces have formed two lines here.

154
00:15:29,640 --> 00:15:31,890
This circle is King Canute.

155
00:15:31,890 --> 00:15:37,370
They've beached their ships, and their
backs are completely undefended.

156
00:15:38,410 --> 00:15:42,500
They know we don't have proper forces.

157
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:49,270
The terrain provides good visibility.
Surprise attacks won't work.

158
00:15:49,270 --> 00:15:51,680
Olmar, how would you attack?

159
00:15:52,510 --> 00:15:56,310
What? U-Uh, at night?

160
00:15:56,310 --> 00:16:01,110
Wrong. Only first-class soldiers
attack at night.

161
00:16:01,110 --> 00:16:04,020
Amateurs can't pull that off.

162
00:16:04,870 --> 00:16:08,690
They're useless pieces of shit.

163
00:16:08,690 --> 00:16:11,280
They'll all be dead by the time
you count to 100.

164
00:16:11,670 --> 00:16:17,020
Wh-What? Then why did
we bother gathering them?

165
00:16:19,150 --> 00:16:20,660
You amateur.

166
00:16:21,040 --> 00:16:23,290
Isn't it obvious?

167
00:16:24,600 --> 00:16:30,030
They'll draw the king's attention
while you're counting to 100.

168
00:16:44,590 --> 00:16:48,270
Thorgil! Where are you, Thorgil?

169
00:16:49,230 --> 00:16:51,900
This is an important moment.

170
00:16:52,910 --> 00:16:55,660
Master, everyone's ready.

171
00:16:55,660 --> 00:16:59,440
All right. Fire on my command.

172
00:17:00,350 --> 00:17:01,770
Draw!

173
00:17:04,250 --> 00:17:07,380
Master, this is my final warning.

174
00:17:08,520 --> 00:17:10,350
If we fight, we'll lose.

175
00:17:11,360 --> 00:17:13,210
Enough, Snake.

176
00:17:13,750 --> 00:17:19,180
The great Iron Fist Ketil is a match
for that youngster in every way.

177
00:17:23,950 --> 00:17:26,000
Fire!

178
00:17:40,880 --> 00:17:42,370
It's started.

179
00:17:46,510 --> 00:17:48,690
Stay safe, Mister Pater.

180
00:17:51,130 --> 00:17:52,060
Damn it!

181
00:17:56,990 --> 00:17:59,220
It's all right. Let's keep going.

182
00:17:59,910 --> 00:18:02,060
Both forces are locked in combat.

183
00:18:04,620 --> 00:18:06,730
Slowly. Try not to shake the wagon.

184
00:18:13,270 --> 00:18:16,080
Don't blame me for whatever happens.

185
00:18:16,080 --> 00:18:19,950
This is theft, isn't it? I'm a thief now...

186
00:18:20,320 --> 00:18:24,270
Don't worry about it.
We left behind enough to pay for her.

187
00:18:25,870 --> 00:18:28,960
You get things done when you need to, huh?

188
00:18:29,390 --> 00:18:33,020
She's Thorfinn's friend.
We can't abandon her.

189
00:18:33,020 --> 00:18:35,930
If she stays here, she'll be killed.

190
00:18:42,490 --> 00:18:46,810
We didn't get to say goodbye
to the old master.

191
00:19:21,790 --> 00:19:24,540
Are the children asleep?

192
00:19:29,720 --> 00:19:30,850
Yes.

193
00:19:32,410 --> 00:19:36,730
The rocking of the cart
puts them to sleep so quickly.

194
00:19:45,110 --> 00:19:46,290
Are you afraid?

195
00:19:48,230 --> 00:19:52,890
Don't worry.
We'll be out of these dark woods soon.

196
00:19:54,910 --> 00:19:59,530
This place is a heap of pain and despair.

197
00:19:59,530 --> 00:20:02,570
A forest of beasts who thirst for blood.

198
00:20:03,270 --> 00:20:05,930
Not a place to foster life.

199
00:20:09,250 --> 00:20:13,570
We have a warm home waiting for us.

200
00:20:15,580 --> 00:20:18,730
It's been a long and difficult road.

201
00:20:19,550 --> 00:20:22,780
But that pain will end soon.

202
00:20:25,210 --> 00:20:26,280
Yes.

203
00:20:28,710 --> 00:20:29,980
You're right.

204
00:20:44,890 --> 00:20:45,970
But...

205
00:20:48,810 --> 00:20:50,490
They're still here.

206
00:20:53,110 --> 00:20:57,250
Lives still try to survive here.

207
00:21:03,160 --> 00:21:04,140
Gardar?

208
00:21:06,650 --> 00:21:13,200
Tell them—the ones who
looked after you—farewell.

209
00:21:18,840 --> 00:21:22,650
I'll be waiting for you here
with the children.

210
00:21:28,380 --> 00:21:29,680
You're right.

211
00:21:30,730 --> 00:21:34,960
I need to thank Einar and the others.

212
00:21:41,520 --> 00:21:43,790
S-Stop! Stop the cart!

213
00:21:45,480 --> 00:21:47,730
It's me. Do you recognize me?

214
00:21:47,730 --> 00:21:49,030
How are you feeling?

215
00:21:52,550 --> 00:21:54,780
Einar...

216
00:22:04,460 --> 00:22:06,410
Advance 50 paces!

217
00:22:06,410 --> 00:22:10,680
Be thorough. Show them your superiority.

218
00:22:22,790 --> 00:22:25,790
The Jomsvikings certainly are impressive.

219
00:22:25,790 --> 00:22:30,140
Not even a single
thin line of 70 men crumbles.

220
00:22:31,240 --> 00:22:33,390
We won't need the rearguard.

221
00:22:33,790 --> 00:22:37,200
Use the second line of thegns to capture Ketil.

222
00:22:37,200 --> 00:22:38,210
Yes, Your Majesty.

223
00:22:38,210 --> 00:22:41,570
Don't retreat! Charge in there!

224
00:22:41,570 --> 00:22:44,330
Show some backbone!

225
00:22:45,920 --> 00:22:50,290
Damn it. Where are my sons?

226
00:23:06,120 --> 00:23:11,470
I c-can't swim with a sword on my back.

227
00:23:17,080 --> 00:23:19,980
I can't do it, Brother.

228
00:23:22,120 --> 00:23:27,130
I can't be like you.

229
00:23:51,640 --> 00:23:55,350
I'm behind you, King Canute.

230
00:25:36,300 --> 00:25:40,050
Pain

231
00:25:38,090 --> 00:25:39,290
"Pain."
